-- WI-907 — two namespaces declaring the SAME short names, so a scope that imports
-- both resolves each one AMBIGUOUSLY. Nothing here references the contested names, so
-- the file loads clean and the conflict is live but unreported until a query names it.
--
-- `cons` deliberately collides with the IMPLICIT TIER (`anthill.prelude.List.cons`);
-- `Widget907` has no tier twin, so the pair covers both halves of the same refusal.
--
-- IT WAS `SortInfo` UNTIL WI-909, which took the eight reflection result sorts off the
-- tier. A name that is no longer a tier spelling makes the tier-collision half of this
-- fixture describe a situation that cannot arise — and the core twin's central row would
-- have gone on PASSING, a ladder with no rung to fall to being unable to fall through.
-- Kept in step with `wi907_ambiguous_name_ladder_test::DECLS`, which repointed the same
-- way and carries the longer argument.
namespace wi907.alpha
  sort cons
    entity si907a(v: anthill.prelude.Int64)
  end
  sort Widget907
    entity w907a(v: anthill.prelude.Int64)
  end
  fact w907a(v: 1)
end

namespace wi907.beta
  sort cons
    entity si907b(v: anthill.prelude.Int64)
  end
  sort Widget907
    entity w907b(v: anthill.prelude.Int64)
  end
  fact w907b(v: 2)
end
